{
  "sn12.32:0.1": "Linked Discourses 12.32 ",
  "sn12.32:0.2": "4. Kaḷāra the Aristocrat ",
  "sn12.32:0.3": "With Kaḷāra the Aristocrat ",
  "sn12.32:1.1": "At Sāvatthī. ",
  "sn12.32:1.2": "Then the mendicant Kaḷāra the Aristocrat went up to Venerable Sāriputta and exchanged greetings with him. ",
  "sn12.32:1.3": "When the greetings and polite conversation were over, he sat down to one side and said to him, ",
  "sn12.32:1.4": "“Reverend Sāriputta, the mendicant Phagguna of the Top-Knot has resigned the training and returned to a lesser life.” ",
  "sn12.32:1.5": "“That venerable mustn’t have gained any solace in this teaching and training.” ",
  "sn12.32:2.1": "“Well then, has Venerable Sāriputta found solace in this teaching and training?” ",
  "sn12.32:3.1": "“Reverend, I have no uncertainty.” ",
  "sn12.32:3.2": "“But what of the future?” ",
  "sn12.32:4.1": "“I have no doubt.” ",
  "sn12.32:5.1": "Then Kaḷāra the Aristocrat went up to the Buddha, bowed, sat down to one side, and said to him, ",
  "sn12.32:5.2": "“Sir, Venerable Sāriputta has declared enlightenment: ",
  "sn12.32:5.3": "‘I understand: “Rebirth is ended, the spiritual journey has been completed, what had to be done has been done, there is nothing further for this place.”’” ",
  "sn12.32:6.1": "So the Buddha addressed one of the monks, ",
  "sn12.32:6.2": "“Please, monk, in my name tell Sāriputta that ",
  "sn12.32:6.3": "the Teacher summons him.” ",
  "sn12.32:6.4": "“Yes, si